<article class="env-lemma" id="00MB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00MB">Lemma <span data-tag="00MB">10.97.2</span>.</a> Let $I$ be an ideal of a Noetherian ring $R$. Denote ${}^\wedge $ completion with respect to $I$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The ring map $R \to R^\wedge $ is flat. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The functor $M \mapsto M^\wedge $ is exact on the category of finitely generated $R$-modules. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Consider $J \otimes _ R R^\wedge \to R \otimes _ R R^\wedge = R^\wedge $ where $J$ is an arbitrary ideal of $R$. According to Lemma <a href="/tag/00MA" data-tag="00MA">10.97.1</a> this is identified with $J^\wedge \to R^\wedge $ and $J^\wedge \to R^\wedge $ is injective. Part (1) follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/00HD" data-tag="00HD">10.39.5</a>. Part (2) is a reformulation of Lemma <a href="/tag/00MA" data-tag="00MA">10.97.1</a> part (2). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>